    "gearCatalogWeaponTurretVulcanDisplayName": "Vulcan Cannon",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsAssaultLore": "A Tri-Tachyon-adjacent blacksite package for breaking defended rooms before the enemy can reorganize. Clean AR-PULSE cells provide the line fire; serial-free GR-SMGs open the breach; a single diverted GRN-FRAG answers massed soft targets without appearing on a corporate manifest.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsAssaultProvenance": "Deniable corporate security",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFieldSecurityLore": "A practical station-security issue for settlements that cannot expect prompt naval help. Twelve ubiquitous Domain-pattern Rooks fill the racks. Specialist weapons are a future technology acquisition, not part of the founding issue.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFieldSecurityProvenance": "Independent frontier",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFireSupportLore": "A low-tech support establishment built to keep firing after a campaign has outlasted its first supply plan. Every team combines the serviceable GR-RFL, an MG-SUPP automatic, and an RL-DMR marksman; old SRM-1 clusters, SRM-3 (Pod) shoulder launchers on two of the automatics and tightly controlled GR-AMRs provide the scarce heavy issue.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFireSupportProvenance": "Ordnance Board auxiliary tables",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLineInfantryLore": "League interoperability means agreeing on cells, ammunition, and fire-team roles without pretending every member world owns the same factories. AR-PULSEs lead, GR-RFLs and MG-SUPPs sustain the line, RL-DMRs exploit open lanes, and GRN-SMK smoke keeps a stalled advance moving.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLineInfantryProvenance": "Kazeron joint standard",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLuddicPathAssaultLore": "Recovered Pather assault tables contain no clean quartermaster's mirror of a state arsenal. Black-market GR-SMGs, old GR-RFLs, industrial DEP-CHG kits, and a scarce captured heavy weapon turn ordinary compartments into close, decisive killing grounds.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLuddicPathAssaultProvenance": "Path cell caches",
