		"debriefSluiceWithdrawnSome": "{0} of Greyhook''s people walked off along the service road on Voss''s order; Berth Four held dispatch until we took it.",
		"debriefSluiceWithdrawnNone": "Nobody we saw made it out along the service road; Berth Four held dispatch until we took it.",
		"debriefSluiceClosingLosses": "We paid for that pier: {0} of ours {0,choice,1#is|1<are} on the roll that won''t come home. Dormer is asking what it would take to keep us here. He wasn''t asking that when we arrived.",
		"debriefSluiceClosingClean": "Everyone we put down at Black Sluice is coming home. Dormer is asking what it would take to keep us here. He wasn't asking that when we arrived.",
		"debriefSluiceHandover": "Customs, fuel control and dispatch are held, the marked fuel storage is intact, and the custody party signed the handover in the control room under {0}. {1}",
		"debriefSluiceAwardPremium": "Your invoice is settled: {0} credits, the 44,000 fee and the 12,000 premium House Custody promised. Black Sluice''s surface facility and its levy route are out of Greyhook''s hands. That is all I will claim for it.",
		"debriefSluiceAwardCompact": "Your invoice is settled: {0} credits, the full 44,000 fee. The compact forwent the premium, as written. Black Sluice''s surface facility and its levy route are out of Greyhook''s hands. That is all I will claim for it.",
		"debriefTermsCostCustody": "Company casualties: {0}. Representatives lost: {1}. Technicians lost: {2}. Estate guards lost: {3}. Constables lost: {4}.",
		"debriefTermsCostFitters": "Company casualties: {0}. Representatives lost: {1}. Technicians lost: {2}. Fitters lost: {3}. Constables lost: {4}.",
		"debriefTermsWhyCarrier": "The records carrier was destroyed. {0}",
		"debriefTermsWhyRepresentatives": "Every custody representative was killed. {0}",
		"debriefTermsWhyTechnicians": "Both technicians were killed before the tooling was commissioned. {0}",
		"debriefTermsWhyNotRatified": "The handover was not ratified. {0}",
		"debriefTermsReplacement": "No fee and no ratification. The signed agreement stands; a new mobilization brings a replacement party and carrier. These losses stay on the account.",
		"debriefTermsDossierCrew": "The captured tooling is commissioned. With Greyhook's own service records we can rebuild their ARM-PIR-3-PWR properly: a light section, two rigs in twelve, and nothing in it you have not seen across the yard today.",
		"debriefTermsDossierCastle": "Neither technician who did the work came back. Their log and the commissioned tooling still make the Boarding Jack dossier; I am reading it from what they left.",
		"debriefTermsRatifiedCustody": "Ratified under House Custody. Bench access passes to Dormer's office; association workshops operate on new leases with debt deductions. The 12,000-credit premium is payable only on Chapter 5 victory.",
		"debriefTermsRatifiedCompact": "Ratified under the Yard Compact. Inspected common-service access continues under the signed repayment schedule; Dormer appoints security and records the company as an independent counterparty. No premium is owed.",
		"debriefTermsAward": "Thirty-two thousand credits. The handover is ratified. The debt and the duty against Greyhook are unchanged.",
		"debriefTermsIssuePending": "The Boarding Jack section card is recorded to the company. Its issue pattern is not ready to print; the card goes to fleet cargo once, when it is. Nobody is refitted automatically.",
		"debriefTermsIssueReady": "Learn the Boarding Jack card from fleet cargo. Fitting it is an explicit Armory choice; nobody is refitted automatically.",
		"debriefTermsClosing": "{0} Dormer names no ship and no date in that letter, and I will not guess at either.",
		"debriefYardCost": "Company casualties: {0}. Inspection technicians lost: {1}. Constables lost: {2}.",
		"debriefYardWithdrawalTooling": "The marked calibration machine was destroyed. {0}",
		"debriefYardWithdrawalIncomplete": "The inspection was not completed. {0}",
		"debriefYardReplacement": "No completion fee or pattern is released. A new mobilization will fund replacement inspectors and tooling refit. This loss stays on the account; no custody agreement has been chosen.",
		"debriefYardAward": "Thirty-six thousand credits and the ARM-HEG-3-PWR (QS) refurbishment pattern. The inspection settles this contract; it does not settle the yard's custody.",
		"debriefYardIssue": "Learn the ARM-HEG-3-PWR (QS) card from fleet cargo. Once both recovered patterns are learned, fit Salvage-assisted Section in the Armory: eight regular marines, two ARM-TACH-3-PWR (QS) breachers and two ARM-HEG-3-PWR (QS) support wearers. Their names and lift seats stay the same; no equipment has changed automatically.",
		"debriefYardOrder": "Dormer's secured claim remains recognized under Combine administration. The yard's arrears are enforceable. Inspection grants neither repossession nor collection authority to this company.",
		"debriefYardLeases": "The outstanding debt remains on the yard account. House Custody would place tool access under Dormer's office, with new workshop leases and debt deductions. These are proposed terms, not a signed instruction.",
		"debriefYardCounterproposal": "Counterproposal: inspected common-service access continues under a signed repayment schedule. Dormer appoints security; the association operates the shops and keeps auditable service allocation. The debt stands.",
		"debriefYardClosing": "{0} Both written agreements are at Company HQ. Read them, ask me to compare them, or leave them for now; nothing is committed until you sign one. The next commission waits on that signature.",
		"debriefWarrantCost": "Company casualties: {0}. Supplier technicians lost: {1}. Constables lost: {2}. Their names stay with this account.",
		"debriefWarrantRecords": "The archive is authenticated and the calibration load is back. We have the files and the tools to use them.",
		"debriefWarrantAward": "Thirty thousand credits, and the ARM-TACH-3-PWR (QS) refurbishment pattern under my supplier guarantee. That settles this recovery contract. It decides nothing about the yard's future management.",
		"debriefWarrantIssue": "Learn the ARM-TACH-3-PWR (QS) card from fleet cargo, then choose Tri-Tachyon Specter Section in the Armory. If we already hold the card or know the pattern, there is no second copy. Nobody's fitting has changed. This is repaired security stock, not military issue; keep someone watching the flank.",
		"debriefWarrantWithdrawal": "{0,choice,0#The service archive was not authenticated.|1#The authenticated service archive is retained.} {1,choice,0#The calibration kit was not returned.|1#The calibration load was destroyed.}",
		"debriefWarrantUnpaid": "No completion fee or pattern is released. I will fund a new calibration load and replacement recovery party when you recommission the work.",
		"debriefWeirCost": "Company casualties: {0}. Constables lost: {1}. Technicians lost: {2}. Keep those people on the record beside the work.",
		"debriefWeirSecured": "The repair load reached the isolation switch. Both rooms are reconnected and the road gun is commissioned. The company resolved the attack; North Weir is working again.",
		"debriefWeirInvoice": "Your invoice is honored: {0} credits. This was security work within my concession; the Combine''s administration remains its own.",
		"debriefWeirClosure": "There is equipment in the Low Quay bonded stores your people could use. I can authorize its release. Read the warrant when you are ready; it covers recovery, not debt enforcement or control of the yard.",
		"debriefWeirWork": "The north room {0,choice,0#was not reconnected|1#was reconnected}; the south room {1,choice,0#was not reconnected|1#was reconnected}. {2,choice,0#No repair-load loss is confirmed.|1#The repair load was destroyed.}",
		"debriefWeirWithdrawal": "North Weir has not been handed over. {0}",
		"debriefWeirUnpaid": "The completion fee is unpaid. A return to North Weir will be a new mobilization: fresh repair cargo and a replacement technician party. No unfinished field work is signed off.",
		"debriefWeirRetry": "Replenish your people and shuttles, and bring a working tender. The contract can wait until your company is ready.",
