    "openingMechLabVehicleNoteCopy": "Fit an engine, a gun, plating and kits from stores; drag a part back to stores to take it off.",
    "openingMechLabScrap": "SCRAP",
    "vehicleLoreHEAVY_APC": "The Hegemony's standard troop carrier, built to a drawing old enough that every yard in the Persean Sector has a jig for it. Six seats, a roof gun, and armour that stops what militias carry. Yards bolt heavier plate and hotter engines onto the same hull for escort work. Nobody loves it; everybody has one.",
    "vehicleLoreBREAKTHROUGH_TANK": "A shape older than anyone's records: a slab of plate, a heavy gun, and as few people inside as possible. The drone swarms of the AI Wars taught every survivor that anything thin dies, and in all the centuries since nobody has found a better answer. The Hegemony builds it to the old drawings with a dumb autoloader doing the work a crew of five once did. Two crew sealed in a box of steel, behind guns big enough to end the argument. Fitted with a point-defence screen it is the Parapet, its launchers and radar swatting rockets out of the air: the only clever thing aboard, and Hegemony crews treat it like a guest, useful, expensive, and the first thing they expect to fail.",
    "vehicleLoreMILITIA_TECHNICAL": "A pickup, a pintle mount and a welder. Every independent world builds these, and every pirate band steals them. It is fast, cheap and gone the moment anything heavier than a rifle notices it.",
    "vehicleLoreFIRE_SUPPORT_APC": "The Lion's Guard took a common APC hull and gave its troop bay to a breech-loading mortar and its ready rounds. The Diktat issues it by allotment and counts every shell. It parks behind the line and makes the line's problems disappear in high arcs; its seats were traded for the tube.",
    "vehicleLoreLASER_TANK": "A breakthrough hull carrying a starship's burst laser where the cannons used to be. In orbit that emitter swats fighters off a cruiser's flank and barely marks proper plate. On the ground almost nothing it meets is proper plate: it sweeps a street in the time a gun tank takes to reload, and it cannot open a wall or kill another tank to save its crew's lives.",
    "vehicleLoreDOZER_BREACHER": "A Hegemony engineering hull the Path took and kept: the gun gone, a blade and a ram in its place, one zealot in a sealed box of plate. Pather cells call it the Plough. Walls fall over when you push them hard enough, and plate does not care what is shooting at it.",
    "vehicleLoreSUPPLY_TRUCK": "A workshop pickup with its bed full of ammunition crates and repair stock. It carries no gun and needs none, as long as it stays behind the people who do.",
    "vehicleLoreSCOUT_CAR": "A pickup with a salvaged sensor mast welded to the cab. It sees farther than anything else in the lance and survives about as well as you would expect of a truck.",
    "vehicleLoreSRM_TECHNICAL": "A stripped pickup carrying one SRM-30 rack. Militias love it because it can kill a tank once. It rarely gets a second try.",
    "vehicleLoreLRM_CARRIER": "The common APC hull carrying a single LRM-15 rack instead of passengers. It sits far back and rains guided salvos on whatever the spotters mark.",
    "vehicleLoreHOVER_SCOUT": "Tri-Tachyon's corporate scout: lift fans, a composite skirt and a sensor cluster worth more than the hull. It skims over ground that bogs down tracks, and it folds like paper when hit.",
    "vehicleLoreDRONE_SKIMMER": "A Tri-Tachyon hover carrier for a small wing of combat drones. The skimmer itself is fragile; its drones are not its only defence, but they are its best one.",
    "openingMechLabSelectToPreview": "Click to preview this pattern on the pad.",
