    "openingCompanyPrologueSecondWind": "SECOND WIND",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheWritingOnTheWall": "THE WRITING ON THE WALL",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWhatWeLeftBehind": "WHAT WE LEFT BEHIND",
    "openingCompanyPrologueRaisingHer": "RAISING HER",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheDepartureRoster": "THE DEPARTURE ROSTER",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSomewhereToDock": "SOMEWHERE TO DOCK",
    "openingCompanyPrologueAWayToSurvive": "A WAY TO SURVIVE",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheCerberusHadBeenTheClaimSEscort": "The Cerberus had been the Claim's escort until the run she came home with her reactor shroud holed and half her crew in the clinic. Raiders, the report said. Fixing her would have cost more than she was worth, so the company stripped her best guns and moored her out in the belt, not worth the scrap. Years of drifting grit did the rest: her frame never sat true again, her drive ran rough, and everything aboard ate spares. You towed her in to the locks with an ore tug. The first time you lit her drive, the coils blew and took the inspection lamps with them. The second time, nothing at all. The days chalked beside her airlock went from twelve to five while you pulled coil out of a hauler that hadn't flown since before the Claim had a name.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheDepartureRosterIsInYourHandwriting": "Cramped as it is, the departure roster holds the names of everyone left on the station. Castle's additions run down the margin in a smaller hand: fuel, seals, filters, one more person who needed a berth, then another. Near the bottom, in block capitals, Morgan Hale has added her escort section: fifteen names, two struck through. While you were checking the last pressure patch, someone painted SECOND WIND over the old registry and didn't sign it.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCorvusFillsTheNavigationDisplay": "Corvus fills the navigation display: working yards, steady freight, Hegemony patrols crawling along the lanes. You plotted for it before the Claim was out of sight, on the promise of a repair berth and a visitor's visa. Now the relay finally answers, and Castle opens a thread that is years old and ends in the middle of an argument: Nessa Venn, Jangala.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueACargoHandSleepsAgainstTheBridgeHatch": "A cargo hand sleeps against the bridge hatch with her boots on. The crew take turns in the bunks that still hold pressure. In the hold, Morgan's twelve sleep in shifts beside their stacked rifles. Below decks are two wrecked Hermes shuttles and compartments you haven't dared put back on the power bus.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueYouCanLetGoOfTheChair": "You can let go of the chair, Commander. The seals are leaking like nothing else, but we have O2 canisters to spare for what we lose, enough to make the last mile. I sent the bridge crew to get some sleep. Half of them are in the galley instead, asking each other what Jangala's like. After nearly a decade in the belt working transplutonic ore shafts, a colossal habitable world that isn't a barren rock has become a thing of myth.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueISignedForEveryOneOfThoseCarriers": "We all saw what was happening back on the station. Shuttles would come in and leave with the higher-ups' families and heavy machinery, and the hauler fleet thinned out in those last weeks. The notice in the canteen was a real blow, but the Nebula that missed its promised pickup date was the last one. I still can't believe it. Do you think they'd really abandon us like that, or was the ship lost?",
    "openingCompanyPrologueEveryoneAboardHasAPocketfulOfScrip": "Everyone aboard has a pocketful of scrip and hardly an actual credit to their name. Over the years I kept back a little in real credits, the kind that spend anywhere in the sector. Not much, but it's what gets us a berth at the yard waiting for us on the planet.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWeGaveHerTheLowerHabsAirPlant": "We gave her the lower habs' air plant to get her sealed. After that there was no going back down. If she hadn't lit on the third try, I'd have been standing in the dark with everyone asking me what next.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSabineDidnTAskIfThereWasRoom": "Morgan didn't ask if there was room. She asked where her people should stand. The two she struck off were down the lower shaft when it went dark. She hasn't said their names since, and I haven't asked.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueAnOldFriendIOweHerMore": "An old friend. I owe her more than she'll let me say. If she's still at Greywater Down, she'll find us a cradle. If she isn't, we're a long way from anyone else who owes me anything. I'll tell you the rest on the way down.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueNessaVennWeRanOreTogetherBefore": "Nessa Venn. We ran ore together before she settled into the yards on Jangala. Once spent three days towing my dead freighter home and swore she'd cut me loose at every buoy. Never did. If she's still at Greywater Down, she'll find us a cradle. If she isn't, we're a long way from anyone else who owes me anything.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueNessaAnsweredSheSHeldACradle": "Nessa answered. She's held a cradle for us, and she'll do the work for what I've saved: bunks and a proper fit, nothing more. After that we're forty-five people in a yard with an empty galley, visitors on a world where we have no licence to immigrate. We'll need work before we go back out into the void, Commander, and soon.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueThenGoAndGetSomeSleepYourself": "Working the belt was steady work.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueYouWerenTTheOneWhoLeft": "We can't know for certain.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueThenItStaysBetweenUsUntilWeLand": "It will allow us to start anew.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSheLit": "She lit.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueThenNobodyElseGetsLeft": "Nobody else gets left behind.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSendIt": "Given our fuel and hull, we're lucky to have made it this far.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTakeUsTo": "Take us to {0}.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCrewAboardSpendableCredits": "Crew {0} / 45 aboard / {1} spendable credits",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheAlarmAboveTheHatchHasFinally": "The odd hiss and creaking bulkhead seal still have the crew on edge. It's a wonder this old wreck is holding pressure, with its cracked bulkheads, faulty scavenged life-support modules and a million leaks from nearly a lifetime adrift in the asteroid belt around the Claim.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueHarkerSClaimWasThreeWeeksHaul": "The ore-rich field was three weeks' haul from the nearest port, and the transplutonic ore in its seams drew the corporations in. Then the good seams thinned, and slowly the Claim stopped paying. The second shaft was \"suspended pending survey.\" The drill rigs went out on the carriers \"for refurbishment\" and never returned. Carriers came monthly instead of weekly. The notice of the Claim's closure went up soon after.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheLastOreCarrierTookTheMine": "The date was when facility support would end: air, heat, power. The last ore carrier left eleven days before it, with the administrators and the payroll aboard. Passage for workers was offered. The rest of the Claim kept reporting for shifts until the ration counter stopped taking company scrip.",
