    "openingRefitTrackBRIG": "Brig",
    "openingRefitTierBRIGDEFICIT": "Sealed brig",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIGDEFICIT": "Sealed compartment, reserved for a brig.",
    "openingRefitTierBRIGRESTORED": "Brig open",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIGRESTORED": "Two holding cells and a guard post.",
    "openingRefitTierBRIGIMPROVED_I": "Interrogation",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIGIMPROVED_I": "Not offered yet: the company takes no prisoners in battle for the brig to question.",
    "openingRefitTierBRIGIMPROVED_II": "Interrogation",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIGIMPROVED_II": "Not offered yet: the company takes no prisoners in battle for the brig to question.",
    "openingRefitReserveOpenCopy": "The yard cut the seals and fitted her out. She is ours to use now.",
    "openingRefitGroupSTORES": "SHIP'S STORES",
    "openingRefitTrackHYDROPONICS": "Hydroponics",
    "openingRefitTierHYDROPONICSDEFICIT": "Dry stores",
    "openingRefitEffectHYDROPONICSDEFICIT": "No grow racks: the provisions store holds dry stores only.",
    "openingRefitTierHYDROPONICSRESTORED": "Grow racks rigged",
    "openingRefitEffectHYDROPONICSRESTORED": "Racks, lights and a water feed in the provisions store; nothing harvested yet.",
    "openingRefitTierHYDROPONICSIMPROVED_I": "Hydroponic racks",
    "openingRefitEffectHYDROPONICSIMPROVED_I": "Her supplies per month -5%.",
    "openingRefitTierHYDROPONICSIMPROVED_II": "Closed-loop farm",
    "openingRefitEffectHYDROPONICSIMPROVED_II": "Her supplies per month -10%.",
    "openingRefitLoreHYDROPONICS": "The provisions store has the headroom for grow racks if we give up some shelving. Racks need light and a water feed off the reclamation loop, so nothing grows until life support and power are sound. Fresh greens will not feed a company, but they stretch what we buy, and a closed loop stretches it further.",
    "openingRefitTrackWARDROOM": "Wardroom",
    "openingRefitTierWARDROOMDEFICIT": "No wardroom",
    "openingRefitEffectWARDROOMDEFICIT": "Officers eat with the company; no staff work aboard.",
    "openingRefitTierWARDROOMRESTORED": "Wardroom",
    "openingRefitEffectWARDROOMRESTORED": "An officers' end of the mess, screened off. Officer XP unchanged.",
    "openingRefitTierWARDROOMIMPROVED_I": "Staff college",
    "openingRefitEffectWARDROOMIMPROVED_I": "Officer XP from missions +15%.",
    "openingRefitTierWARDROOMIMPROVED_II": "War college",
    "openingRefitEffectWARDROOMIMPROVED_II": "Officer XP from missions +30%.",
    "openingRefitLoreWARDROOM": "The far end of the mess, screened off, with a table and a locker of manuals. Officers who argue over the last landing before the next one learn faster than those who only live through it. Put war-game consoles on the cluster and it becomes a staff college.",
    "openingRefitTrackBRIEFING": "Briefing room",
    "openingRefitTierBRIEFINGDEFICIT": "No briefing room",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIEFINGDEFICIT": "Orders go out over the mess tables.",
    "openingRefitTierBRIEFINGRESTORED": "Briefing corner",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIEFINGRESTORED": "A briefing end of the mess, with a screen and seating.",
    "openingRefitTierBRIEFINGIMPROVED_I": "Plot table",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIEFINGIMPROVED_I": "A plot table in the briefing corner; the holo-tank is built on it. No battle effect yet.",
    "openingRefitTierBRIEFINGIMPROVED_II": "Holo-tank",
    "openingRefitEffectBRIEFINGIMPROVED_II": "Holo-tank: the briefing shows the garrison the operation faces.",
    "openingRefitLoreBRIEFING": "The other end of the mess, cleared for a screen and seating so orders stop going out over the soup. A plot table, and later a holo-tank run off the processing cluster, would let squads walk the ground before they land on it.",
    "openingRefitTrackHOLDS": "Holds",
    "openingRefitTierHOLDSDEFICIT": "Loose stowage",
    "openingRefitEffectHOLDSDEFICIT": "Cargo lashed where it fits; capacity as converted.",
    "openingRefitTierHOLDSRESTORED": "Holds restowed",
    "openingRefitEffectHOLDSRESTORED": "Holds surveyed and restowed; capacity as converted.",
    "openingRefitTierHOLDSIMPROVED_I": "Racked holds",
    "openingRefitEffectHOLDSIMPROVED_I": "Cargo capacity +20.",
    "openingRefitTierHOLDSIMPROVED_II": "Bonded stores",
    "openingRefitEffectHOLDSIMPROVED_II": "Cargo capacity +40.",
    "openingRefitTrackRESERVE_HANGAR": "Reserve hangar",
    "openingRefitTierRESERVE_HANGARDEFICIT": "No reserve",
    "openingRefitEffectRESERVE_HANGARDEFICIT": "Every machine aboard stands on a working berth or gantry.",
    "openingRefitTierRESERVE_HANGARRESTORED": "Reserve hangar",
    "openingRefitEffectRESERVE_HANGARRESTORED": "Stores 2 whole machines off their berths and gantries.",
    "openingRefitTierRESERVE_HANGARIMPROVED_I": "Racked reserve",
    "openingRefitEffectRESERVE_HANGARIMPROVED_I": "Stores 4 whole machines off their berths and gantries.",
    "openingRefitTierRESERVE_HANGARIMPROVED_II": "Racked reserve",
    "openingRefitEffectRESERVE_HANGARIMPROVED_II": "Stores 4 whole machines off their berths and gantries.",
    "openingRefitLoreRESERVE_HANGAR": "Behind the shuttle deck is a sealed bay the conversion never finished. Cleared and lit, it holds machines the company wants to keep but not fly: fit, callsign and repair clock untouched. Racked two high on cradles, it holds twice as many.",
    "openingRefitLoreHOLDS": "The conversion took a good share of her cargo space for berths, and what is left is stowed by whoever loaded last. Racking the holds wins it back. Bonded stores, sealed cages with their own climate, win more, if the workshop can cut the frames.",
    "openingRefitLorePOWER": "Her reactor is older than anyone aboard and still sound. The trouble is the distribution trunk behind it: decades of splices feeding compartments it was never rated for. Every system on this tree draws through that trunk, which is why the yard wants it done first.",
    "openingRefitLoreLIFE_SUPPORT": "Scrubbers, water reclamation and the thermal loop that keeps the hull from freezing or cooking us. The scrubbers run on recycled filter stock and the air tastes of it. Wounded heal slower in bad air, and nothing that houses more people opens until the loop can carry them.",
    "openingRefitLoreSTRUCTURE": "She took a hit through the dorsal spine before she was ours. The yard bridged it with welded bracing, which holds, but the bulkheads along that line flex under burn. Until the spine is trued nobody signs off on new plating, drive work or anything heavy bolted to a deck.",
    "openingRefitLoreCOMPUTE": "Every console aboard answers to one core cluster behind the bridge. Half its boards are dead and the rest run degraded, so screens go dark and the plot lags the sensors. Rebuilt, it runs the ship. With AI hardware in the rack it starts to fight like a warship.",
    "openingRefitLoreFABRICATION": "The workshop under the parts cage: lathes, a printer bed and the gantry the mech lab borrows. It is restored from its own card on the deck, not from here, but the plating and auxiliary plant further down the tree are cut on its machines.",
    "openingRefitLoreMESS": "Galley, cold store and the long tables. Marines will live on field rations for a long time, but a hot meal at a table together is how a company remembers it is one. Morale comes back faster with a working galley behind it.",
    "openingRefitLoreGYM": "A sealed hold aft of the quarters, sized for a gym and a running loop. Weeks between landings cost muscle and edge, and a squad that drills aboard steps off the shuttle ready.",
    "openingRefitLoreSICK_BAY": "The plans call for a ward, a clinic and a rehab pool. Today the wounded recover in their racks while the medic does rounds. A real bay needs steady power and clean air before the seals come off.",
    "openingRefitLoreREC_LOUNGE": "Seating, a card table and a small chapel the last owners never finished. It costs little and buys a lot: somewhere for off-watch crew to actually be off watch.",
    "openingRefitLoreBRIG": "Two holding cells and a guard post on the spine, where the bracing is heaviest. A prisoner taken on contract is worth more aboard and alive than left on a planet.",
    "openingRefitLoreRANGE": "Three lanes cut through a reserved hold, baffled and armored. Squads can trial a loadout aboard instead of learning on the drop that the sights are off. It needs power for the target gear and a sound frame to stop a stray round.",
    "openingRefitLoreHULL": "Her plating is a patchwork of salvage, and the armor belts were stripped for scrap before the conversion. In a fleet action she folds early. New plate needs a trued spine first; military belts later need the workshop to cut them.",
    "openingRefitLoreFLUX": "Flux is what lets her shoot and shield at once: the grid soaks the heat of both and the vents dump it. Ours is a merchant grid run past its rating, so she overloads fast. Rebuilding it needs a steady plant, and a military grid wants an alpha core to balance it.",
    "openingRefitLoreSENSORS": "The mast is wired to a cluster that cannot keep up, so she sees short and late. With Compute restored the mast runs at its rating; past that, the tactical core lets it sort contacts and keep her own emissions quiet.",
    "openingRefitLoreDRIVE": "Her drive was detuned after the last owners ran it hot, so she is slow off the mark and a burn behind the fleet. A drive refit needs steady power and a frame that will not twist under thrust.",
    "openingRefitTrackMECH_CALIBRATION": "Mech calibration",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_CALIBRATIONDEFICIT": "No calibration bench",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_CALIBRATIONDEFICIT": "Fire control set by hand on the gantry: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_CALIBRATIONRESTORED": "Calibration bench",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_CALIBRATIONRESTORED": "A bench and boresight rig in the Mech Lab: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_CALIBRATIONIMPROVED_I": "Fire-control calibration",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_CALIBRATIONIMPROVED_I": "Mech weapon accuracy +3%.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_CALIBRATIONIMPROVED_II": "Tactical core link",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_CALIBRATIONIMPROVED_II": "Mech weapon accuracy +6%; torso traverse +25%, onto a new target faster.",
    "openingRefitTrackMECH_COOLANT": "Mech coolant plant",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_COOLANTDEFICIT": "No coolant plant",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_COOLANTDEFICIT": "Heat sinks charged from a hose line: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_COOLANTRESTORED": "Coolant plant",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_COOLANTRESTORED": "A charging plant on the gantry: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_COOLANTIMPROVED_I": "Chilled charge",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_COOLANTIMPROVED_I": "Mech flux dissipation +10%.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_COOLANTIMPROVED_II": "Cryogenic charge",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_COOLANTIMPROVED_II": "Mech flux dissipation +20%.",
    "openingRefitTrackMECH_ARMOR": "Mech armor shop",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_ARMORDEFICIT": "No armor shop",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_ARMORDEFICIT": "Plate patched where it cracked: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_ARMORRESTORED": "Armor shop",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_ARMORRESTORED": "A plate press beside the gantries: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_ARMORIMPROVED_I": "Fitted plate",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_ARMORIMPROVED_I": "Mech section armor +5% at deployment.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_ARMORIMPROVED_II": "Laminated plate",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_ARMORIMPROVED_II": "Mech section armor +10% at deployment.",
    "openingRefitTrackMECH_REPAIR": "Mech field repair",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_REPAIRDEFICIT": "No repair crew",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_REPAIRDEFICIT": "Repairs done between other jobs: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_REPAIRRESTORED": "Repair crew",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_REPAIRRESTORED": "A standing repair crew for the gantries: neutral.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_REPAIRIMPROVED_I": "Repair jigs",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_REPAIRIMPROVED_I": "Damaged mechs repair between missions 25% faster.",
    "openingRefitTierMECH_REPAIRIMPROVED_II": "Spares rack",
    "openingRefitEffectMECH_REPAIRIMPROVED_II": "Repairs 25% faster; a lost mount's replacement weapon costs 25% less to fabricate.",
    "openingRefitTrackVEHICLE_BAY": "Vehicle bay",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYDEFICIT": "Vehicle bay",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYDEFICIT": "Company vehicles cannot deploy yet; no refit is offered.",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYRESTORED": "Vehicle bay",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYRESTORED": "Engine tuning (not yet offered).",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_I": "Turret calibration",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_I": "Turret calibration (not yet offered).",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_II": "Field repair",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_II": "Field repair (not yet offered).",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_CALIBRATION": "A mech's fire control is only as true as the last time someone boresighted it, and on a gantry with dead consoles that means a sergeant with a sight picture and a wrench. A bench wired into the cluster lets the Lab align every mount to the targeting suite between drops. Link it to the tactical core and the pilots get its target sort as well, so the torso is already swinging before they have picked the next one.",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_COOLANT": "Mechs fight on flux, and what decides how long they can keep firing is how cold their sinks go into the drop. Right now we charge them from a hose line off the scrubber loop. A plant of its own on the gantry chills the charge properly, and the reactor overhaul gives it the power to go colder still.",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_ARMOR": "Mech plate comes out of the workshop in standard sheets and gets bolted on as it comes. A press beside the gantries lets the Lab shape and fit each section to its frame and lap the joints, so a round meets more plate where it lands. It needs the workshop's tooling to cut it and a frame that will take the press.",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_REPAIR": "A damaged mech waits in its gantry until somebody has time for it, and every part comes off the workshop's queue. A standing crew with proper jigs turns a repair round in days instead of a week. With a rack of spares cut ahead of time, a mount shot off on the ground is a refit rather than a new build.",
    "openingRefitLoreVEHICLE_BAY": "The gantries can berth a vehicle as well as a mech, but the company cannot field its own yet. When it can, the bay gets its own refits: engine tuning, turret calibration and a repair line. Until then there is nothing here to buy.",
