    "openingCerberusCompanyStartYourCompanyIsReadyCommanderTheFirst": "If the authorities ask, we're completing last mile delivery with the transplutonic dust from our hold, Commander. Zoey's signed off on the shipping label.",
    "openingCerberusCompanyStartOurShipIsHomeNowStayDocked": "She's ours now, Commander, properly. Stay docked while we use the prepaid stores: settle Morgan's first specialty in Barracks, then muster her squad in the Armory and put it under her. I'll take you through each order.",
    "openingCerberusCompanyStartAnAccessiblePlanetarySpaceport": "an accessible planetary spaceport",
    "openingCerberusCompanyStartCrossingFuel": "Castle: Our port is closed to us, so we make for {0}. I''ve topped up the tanks with the {1} fuel it takes to get there.",
    "secondWindKeepLostBattle": "Castle: We've lost Second Wind, Commander. Salvagers will have her off the field before the wreck cools. Any port with a yard can get her back to us; ask for Marine operations there.",
    "secondWindKeepLostMarket": "Castle: Second Wind is gone from the fleet, Commander. Ships like her turn up again. When she does, any port with a yard can get her back to us; ask for Marine operations there.",
    "secondWindKeepBoughtBack": "Castle: Second Wind is back with the fleet. Welcome home, Commander.",
    "secondWindKeepAwayLost": "Second Wind is gone. Any port with a spaceport can sell her back for {0} credits: open Marine operations there. Until she is back, Company HQ is closed and campaign missions cannot be flown.",
    "secondWindKeepAwayInStorage": "Second Wind is in storage at {0}. Take her out of storage to bring the company home. Until then Company HQ and Marine operations are closed.",
    "secondWindKeepAwayUnknown": "Second Wind is not with the fleet. Until she is back Company HQ and Marine operations are closed.",
    "secondWindKeepMissionLost": "Campaign missions are flown from Second Wind. Buy her back at any port with a yard (Marine operations) first.",
    "secondWindKeepMissionStored": "Campaign missions are flown from Second Wind. Take her out of storage first.",
    "secondWindKeepMissionNotAboard": "Campaign missions are flown from Second Wind. Move the company back aboard her (Ship Transfer) first.",
    "secondWindBuyBackOption": "Second Wind",
    "secondWindBuyBackOptionTooltip": "Castle has found Second Wind. Buy her back here.",
    "secondWindBuyBackNoYard": "No yard here can sell Second Wind back. Try a port with a spaceport.",
    "secondWindBuyBackHeading": "SECOND WIND",
    "secondWindBuyBackBattleTitle": "Towed In",
    "secondWindBuyBackBattleCaption": "A salvage yard's berth, and a hull everyone here already knows.",
    "secondWindBuyBackBattleNarrative": "Salvagers pulled {0} off the field and sold her on to a yard, still smoking. The yard has patched what it could and kept the rest as a scar.",
    "secondWindBuyBackBattleDialogue": "I made some calls, Commander. They know whose she is, and they know we will pay. They will bring her round to us.",
    "secondWindBuyBackMarketTitle": "On the Open Market",
    "secondWindBuyBackMarketCaption": "A broker's listing, three lines long, and one of them is her name.",
    "secondWindBuyBackSoldNarrative": "{0} went to the breakers'' list the day we sold her. Nobody wanted an old Cerberus with her history, and she was still on it.",
    "secondWindBuyBackScuttledNarrative": "We stripped {0} and left her hull to drift. Somebody towed it in, and somebody else put it back together, after a fashion.",
    "secondWindBuyBackOtherNarrative": "{0} left us. Ships like her do not stay lost for long; this one turned up on a broker''s list.",
    "secondWindBuyBackMarketDialogue": "Look what I found on the open market, Commander. Your ship. The broker will bring {0} round to us, for a price.",
    "secondWindBuyBackDMod": "She comes back with one more scar: {0}.",
    "secondWindBuyBackNoDMod": "She carries all the scars a hull can take; this one left no new mark.",
    "secondWindBuyBackBill": "Price {0} credits. Account {1}; {2} left after.",
    "secondWindBuyBackBillDebt": "Price {0} credits. Account {1}; the {2} short becomes debt at the month''s end.",
    "secondWindBuyBackDestination": "Until she is back, campaign missions cannot be flown.",
    "secondWindBuyBackNote": "She rejoins the fleet here, repaired and crewed.",
    "secondWindBuyBackBuy": "Buy her back: {0} cr",
    "secondWindBuyBackLeave": "Not now",
    "openingCerberusStartTooltip": "You and the rest of the undesirables were abandoned by corporate on a mining rig. You've jury-rigged a mothballed wreck to fly you and your people out. No licence, no patron, four hundred and seventy-three credits. Build a mercenary company from nothing.",
    "openingCerberusStartStory": "The operator's last ore carrier left with the administrators, the payroll, and the medical stores. No ships returned for you and the remaining families and crew. Before supplies ran out you managed to furnish enough spare parts to bring an old abandoned Cerberus online. With a chance of survival restored, the ship was named the Second Wind, and people prepared to depart for a new life after nearly a decade in the belt. Somewhere between the locks and the jump point, they started calling you Commander. You have 473 credits, a down payment Castle will not let anyone touch, twelve unpaid security personnel, and a port berth waiting on Jangala. This start replaces the Galatia tutorial with the Second Wind prologue and Marines Mod company campaign start.",
    "openingSecondWindNexStartStory": "The operator's last ore carrier left with the administrators, the payroll, and the medical stores. No ships returned for you and the remaining families and crew. Before supplies ran out you managed to furnish enough spare parts to bring an old abandoned Cerberus online. With a chance of survival restored, the ship was named the Second Wind, and people prepared to depart for a new life after nearly a decade in the belt. Somewhere between the locks and the jump point, they started calling you Commander. You have 473 credits, a down payment Castle will not let anyone touch, twelve unpaid security personnel, and a port berth waiting on Jangala.",
    "openingCerberusCompanyStartFirstWeNeedMercenaryCompanyConversionOur": "First, the conversion: barracks and a workshop, built into her for good. The yard has the estimate. {0}Choose Return, dock at {1} and open Marine operations from the planet menu; I''ll have the yard order waiting. It isn''t in the standard Refit picker, and Additional Berthing won''t do it. Nothing gets designated until the yard has done its work. Our prepaid stores will wait in the planetary depot.",
    "openingCerberusCompanyStartIHaveKeptThatPaymentSeparateFrom": "My chits pay for it, not the ship's account. The yard takes them even if the account is empty. ",
    "openingCerberusCompanyStartTheConversionIsInstalledStayDockedAt": "The conversion is in. Stay docked at {0}, open Marine operations and name our Cerberus the company''s command ship. While we''re docked here, the preparation bills draw on our depot stock. Then we settle Morgan''s appointment and put her section on the roll.",
