		"auxiliaryWarrantOffered": "Hegemony procurement has sent terms of auxiliary enrolment. Read them at Company HQ.",
		"auxiliaryWarrantResume": "HEGEMONY PROCUREMENT  /  Terms of auxiliary enrolment await an answer",
		"auxiliaryWarrantTitle": "HEGEMONY AUXILIARY WARRANT  /  TERMS OF ENROLMENT",
		"auxiliaryWarrantFrom": "Office of Auxiliary Procurement, Hegemony Fleet Command",
		"auxiliaryWarrantRecord": "This office has read HSS Resolute's after-action report from Garnir, which records that the company's evidence put the cruiser's guns on a pirate battery, and the company's Agreus service as a recovered-suit section under civil terms. On that record it offers enrolment as a Hegemony auxiliary.",
		"auxiliaryWarrantGrants": "ON ACCEPTANCE: a military warrant naming the Hegemony Auxiliary Section card, the section in approved ARM-HEG-4-PWR (MSL) suits. The Hegemony licence channel may then offer it.\nAFTER THE FIRST OBLIGATION PERIOD IS HONOURED: the warrant adds the Hegemony Shock card, in ARM-HEG-4-PWR pattern.",
		"auxiliaryWarrantObligations": "OBLIGATIONS: in each obligation period, complete a contract for the Hegemony or answer its service call. Take no contract against the Hegemony, and keep relations at Favorable or better. A missed period stops its cards going to any further squad until the next honoured one; nothing learned is revoked.",
		"auxiliaryWarrantLimits": "THIS WARRANT DOES NOT GRANT: any other tradition's Restricted equipment; release of military suits to the company's polity; Hegemony command authority; immunity from Hegemony law.",
		"auxiliaryWarrantDeclineNote": "Declining is final for these terms. Every other route stays open, including a standing warrant earned later.",
		"auxiliaryWarrantAccept": "ACCEPT ENROLMENT",
		"auxiliaryWarrantDecline": "DECLINE",
		"auxiliaryWarrantLater": "CLOSE / LATER",
		"auxiliaryWarrantDone": "CLOSE",
		"auxiliaryWarrantAcceptedTitle": "HEGEMONY AUXILIARY WARRANT  /  ENROLMENT RECORDED",
		"auxiliaryWarrantAcceptedCopy": "The company is enrolled as a Hegemony auxiliary. The Hegemony Auxiliary Section card is open to it through the Hegemony licence channel, and the warrant stands on the company record at HQ.\nThe Hegemony Shock card follows the first honoured obligation period. Keep the terms once, and this office will write again.",
		"auxiliaryWarrantDeclinedTitle": "HEGEMONY AUXILIARY WARRANT  /  TERMS DECLINED",
		"auxiliaryWarrantDeclinedCopy": "Your answer is recorded. This office will not repeat these terms. The company keeps every other route to approved equipment, including the standing warrant the Hegemony grants to companies it trusts closely.",
		"arcIssueListedRelief": "Stocked at the Wayline broker's market after the relief.",
		"arcIssueListedThunderRun": "Stocked by the route's employer after Thunder Run.",
		"arcIssueListedBlindWatch": "Stocked at Hegemony markets after Blind Watch.",
		"arcIssueListedWorkingPassage": "Stocked at Asharu after the Morrow's Working Passage.",
		"equipmentTemplateAccessCommonRoute": "Common templates may circulate through unrestricted faction markets.",
		"equipmentTemplateAccessGatedRouteFmt": "Licensed and patron access requires MRB +{0}; high-risk recovery requires {1} company victories. Licensed stock also requires Favorable standing with the selling faction.",
		"nexInvadeForkText": "How will this invasion be fought? Marine Operations lands the company and fights it out now, on the ground, and the result stands when the battle ends: no time for fleets to intervene. Nexerelin fights its own ground battle over several days.",
		"nexInvadeForkMarine": "Fight it with Marine Operations",
