	"agreusGuideRouteSettled": "Marine operations > {0} / {1} on the Low Quay freight lane",
	"agreusGuideRouteRatified": "Marine operations > Baronet Elian Dormer / A Small War at Black Sluice",
	"agreusGuideRouteDefault": "Learn both recovered-suit cargo cards, then fit Salvage-assisted Section in the Armory.",
	"agreusGuidePrepOpen": "Signing commits one route and closes the other. You may instead decline further work and keep completed fees and cards.",
	"agreusGuidePrepSettled": "{0}: “{1}” Escort postings recur: two squads, fitted shuttles; each consignment is new freight and new people.",
	"agreusGuidePrepRatified": "Three full squads recommended, fitted shuttles and working tender. Take customs, fuel control and dispatch; preserve the marked fuel tanks. Optional owned mech.",
	"agreusGuidePrepSigned": "{0}: “{1}”",
	"agreusGuidePrepComplete": "Issued gear is unchanged. Already learned or carried cards satisfy the award; selling a card does not renew it. Recovered equipment is below military issue.",
	"corvusDustLedgerTitle": "The Dust Ledger",
	"corvusDustLedgerBriefing": "We have spent enough contracts reacting to their attacks. This time we choose where to go. The Sable crew buys departure times from a broker on Asharu. Their inland counting house holds the dispatch archive. Seize the marked high-value target and return to the extraction point with the records. We need their buyers, not a fight with Asharu's authorities.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebrief": "The archive names a listening post on Warion. Sable has been matching our manifests to intercepted departure calls. Our own schedules are in it too, released under Jack Prell's dispatch authority. The last batch is dated the week he left. He built Wayline. I don't understand why he would sell it, and I don't know who he sold it for. You brought back a target we can act on. Put your company in order; when you are ready, we can take that link away.",
	"corvusDustLedgerTarget": "Ledger room",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief01": "Saltwell Cross, Captain. It's a dust-road trading post on Asharu, where the crawler road from the salvage claims meets the road to the public freight apron. The broker who trades in our sailing times works there: Oskar Teague, out of the old pump house at the east edge of town. He sells them to a pirate crew called Sable.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief02": "Asharu is not ours and not the pirates'. Who comes down on us when the shooting starts?",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief03": "Nobody in particular. The Hegemony claims the world and keeps no administration on it; its patrols turn up to chase pirates or collect tariffs. Wayline lands freight at Saltwell Cross on a schedule, so we come down as the scheduled drop, on the public apron, lawfully.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief04": "And the target is a pirate crew, the one thing the only patrols out here exist to chase. The Hegemony would thank us, if it noticed.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief05": "The town has a market warden, Tobias Ankrum. He speaks for Saltwell Cross, not for Asharu and not for any faction. I bought his indifference with a season of freight credit. His price is that the fight stays at the pump house and the market is not touched.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief06": "Then the market is off the table. Not a round into it, not a stall knocked over. We walk in as freight, not as a raid.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief07": "Teague keeps a skimmer on a pad past the southern canal crossing, and his lift-off is on a schedule. Let it run out and he leaves, and he radios the alarm on his way up. If you take him alive, he can name every buyer he ever sold our dates to.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief08": "The quiet is the resource, Captain, and it spends. A shot fired, or one of us seen by a sentry inside the compound ring, and clerks start feeding the ledger to a burn barrel. Seize the ledger room and the burn stops.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief09": "There are two more favours you can do before that, both outside the ring. Anneke Harrow's crew is stranded in their yard on the crawler road waiting on a drive coupling that is in this drop. Carry it to them and they will be on the crawler road when it starts. Or stand at the warden's well house a while and let Ankrum's watch see you pay your respects: they will hold the cantina and put spotters on the rooftops.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief10": "These cost clock, not exposure. How much of Teague's time you spend on them is your call.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief11": "I want the ledger whole, but I'll take what's left. Even a burned ledger leaves the strongbox, and the strongbox is where the signature will be. Bring the records to the freight apron, and Teague with them if you've got him.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief12": "Records and the broker to the apron. Every surviving squad aboard. Mind the market, Captain.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief13": "One thing more. The compound has gun nests and manned pillboxes on its entrances. The nests are powered, and our manifests show generator parts going in, but not where Sable draws the current. If your squads find it, Captain, it is worth a look.",
	"corvusDustLedgerBrief14": "Find their power before the shooting and the nests may go dark. After it starts, rockets or the Hound answer them. The pillboxes are manned, so those we take by hand.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldFeedApproach": "That's the junction box. Work it quietly and without a break, Captain. If we're pulled off it halfway, the tap stays live.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldFeedFound": "There's their power. A tap off the town's old line, run to a junction box outside the ring. Work it quietly and the nests go dark.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldFeedCut": "The tap's cut. Whatever Sable has pointed at that road is running on batteries and prayer now. Nobody in town will miss it.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldNestsDark": "Gun nests are dark. Their feed stayed cut. Move while they're blind.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldFeedLapsed": "Nests are live. The tap was never cut, and they have the yard covered. Stay off open ground, or bring rockets to bear.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldNestDestroyed": "Nest is down. One fewer gun on that approach. Keep moving.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldPillboxContact": "Pillbox, firing from the slits. They have cover and we don't. Don't trade rounds with it from the open; go round or put something heavy through the slit.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldHarrowCrate": "That crate is Harrow's drive coupling. Their yard is up the crawler road, past the market. Anneke Harrow has been sitting on a dead crawler for nine days, and she has been very civil about it.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldHarrowDelivered": "Harrow has the coupling in and the crawler is turning over. Anneke says her crew will be on the crawler road when it starts, and that this isn't charity, it's an account settled.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldWardenApproach": "That's the well house. Ankrum's the one on the step with the ledger under his arm. Take your time, Captain; we're here to be seen paying respects.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldWardenNod": "Ankrum has nodded. His watch will hold the cantina, and there are watchmen on two market rooftops who'll tell you what they see in the compound yard. That is all he's selling, and it is more than I hoped.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldClockShort": "Captain, Teague's lift-off is close. If you want him, the time to decide is now.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldAlarmShot": "Shots fired. The quiet is over. Civilians are running, so mind your fire.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldAlarmSighted": "A sentry has us inside the ring. Compound is waking up. Go loud and go fast.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldAlarmClock": "Teague's skimmer is up. He's calling it in on his way out. The alarm's on you now, Captain.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldCantinaJoins": "Cantina's emptying. Pirates, a handful of them, heading for the compound with their jackets over their guns.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldCantinaHeld": "Cantina's quiet. The watch has the door and nobody's coming out of it.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldLedgerBurning": "The barrel's lit. They're feeding the books to it a shelf at a time. Seize that ledger room before there's nothing left to seize.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldLedgerHalf": "Half the books are ash, Captain. Whatever's left, take it.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldLedgerSeized": "Ledger room is ours. The burn is stopped. Get what survives to the apron.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldLedgerBurned": "The books are gone. Smoke, nothing else. The strongbox is still in the pump house, and the strongbox is what I need now.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldSalvageTeam": "Harrow's crew is coming down the crawler road. Four of them with rifles, heading for the east gate. They won't last long on their own, so keep the gate busy.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldReserveArrives": "Sable's reserve is on the crawler road: two squads and a Hound with a light gun, running for the pump house. They'll sit on the ledger room. Expect them inside the yard.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldSpotters": "Rooftop watchmen have the compound yard. Marking sentries and the barrel now.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldBrokerFlees": "Teague's out of his office and running for the skimmer pad, south past the canal crossing. Cut him off if you can.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldBrokerSurrendered": "Teague's hands are up. He'll walk with us. Somebody get him to the apron before his friends find him.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldBrokerLost": "We've lost Teague. Whatever he knew has gone with him.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldBrokerBoarded": "The skimmer's off the pad with Teague aboard. That's gone, Captain. Take the records and go.",
	"corvusDustLedgerFieldBrokerApron": "Teague is at the apron, alive. Keep him that way until he's aboard.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefOpenFull": "The ledger room was ours before the barrel did more than smoke. Every book is in the crates, Zoey.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefOpenPartial": "We took the room with the barrel half fed. Half the books are ash, half are in the crates.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefOpenStrongbox": "They fed the barrel faster than we could cross the yard, and the books are ash. We got the strongbox out of the pump house.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefFindFullCaught": "Teague talked before the kettle boiled, and the books agree with him. Every sailing Sable bought is there, Wayline's own schedules, released under Jack Prell's dispatch authority, the last batch dated the week he left. The routing points to a listening post on Warion. I built half of those schedules beside him. I can't tell you why he would sell them.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefFindFullEscaped": "Teague is gone, but the books he couldn't burn tell it without him. Wayline's own schedules, released under Jack Prell's dispatch authority, the last batch dated the week he left. The routing points to a listening post on Warion. He built Wayline. I don't know who he sold it for.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefFindPartialCaught": "The books are scorched and half gone, but Teague filled the gaps and the pages that remain agree with him. Our schedules went out under Jack Prell's dispatch authority, the last of them the week he left. The routing ends at a listening post on Warion. I don't understand it, and he can't tell me why.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefFindPartialEscaped": "Half a ledger and no broker. What survived still carries Jack Prell's dispatch authority on our schedules, the last batch dated the week he left, and the routing that remains names a listening post on Warion. It's enough to act on. It isn't enough to understand.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefFindStrongboxCaught": "The books are ash, but the strongbox wasn't, and Teague has the rest in his head. One page carries Jack Prell's dispatch authority over our schedules, dated the week he left. Teague says the calls went to a listening post on Warion. He doesn't know why Prell did it either.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefFindStrongboxEscaped": "Ash, and Teague in the wind. The strongbox gave us one page, but it is the right one: our schedules released under Jack Prell's dispatch authority, dated the week he left, and a listening post on Warion at the end of the route. I will take that and be glad of it.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefCloseCaught": "Teague is in the hold in one piece, and Ankrum's market came through untouched. That credit was well spent. Put the company in order. When you are ready, we take Warion's ears away.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebriefCloseEscaped": "Teague is out there with his own copy of the numbers. Sable will know we came down as freight. Better to reach Warion before they close their ears. Account for your people first, Captain.",
	"corvusBlindWatchTitle": "Blind Watch",
	"corvusBlindWatchBriefing": "Sable's listening post on Warion, the Sounding, is blind toward Barad. Land behind the moon and plant charges at its three installations: the ranging mast spots for their mortar and rocket battery, the uplink warns Garnir from the alarm, and the dish field is the target. Warion is airless and nobody governs it, so no one else will come, but the strongbox's roster says the post is dug in: pickets and cannon on every approach, and its hardest hands at the gate. The order you take the sites in is the plan.",
	"corvusBlindWatchRequirements": "{0} squads and {1} mechs or vehicles recommended. The Sounding is dug in against armour: pickets and cannon emplacements on all three approaches, a rocket battery that fires on whatever the ranging mast sees, and a plated crawler and a rocket truck on the crater floor. Infantry alone will not get through. Minimum: two squads with four ready marines each. Up to four fitted company shuttles can ferry the selected force. Wayline provides heavy lift for your active mech lance; select Mech Support. No fighter cover or employer infantry.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebrief": "The Sounding is silent. Its mast, uplink and dishes are wrecked, and the routing tables in its signals racks point to Sable's dispatch compound on Garnir. This contract is paid. Account for your people before the company plans its next move.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief01": "Warion, Captain. A small dead moon of Barad's, no air, no town, nobody's flag. Sable has a listening post in a crater on the side that faces away from the gas giant. Their crews call it the Sounding. It is where our departures from Jangala have been heard.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief02": "Who governs it? Who answers when the shooting starts?",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief03": "Nobody. Nobody lives on Warion and no patrol lands there. There is no market to mind this time and no warden to pay. Only Sable's people in their suits and modules, and the people they hired.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief04": "Then what we know about them is all we have. What did Teague's strongbox give us?",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief05": "Where the post is, how to approach it, and their watch roster. A watch boss, Ivo Brannick, and about two dozen security hands, none of them good. Four or five hired signals technicians under a contract chief, Odile Fenner, who run the dishes. They are not fighters; they will keep to the hab.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief06": "Every post has a side it can't watch. Which is theirs?",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief07": "Barad's. The post listens outward, at the system, and the gas giant drowns everything on its own side. They cannot hear or see toward it. We come in behind the moon and land over the horizon, behind a low ridge on the crater's Barad side.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief08": "Then they won't know we are there until they see us, and that is ours to spend. A shot, a sentry, or their ranging mast picking one of us up, and the post wakes.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief09": "Three installations, and they do not do the same work. The ranging mast on the rim watches the ground around the post. While it stands, their mortar carrier can put shells on anything the mast sees, anywhere on the flat.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief10": "Blind it first and the rest gets cheaper. And the second?",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief11": "The uplink, on its knoll to the south-east. It passes what the post hears to Garnir. From the moment of the alarm they will be sending Garnir a warning. If it finishes, Garnir knows we are coming, and that cannot be taken back.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief12": "So the order is the plan, Captain. Mast first makes the crossing cheap and probably costs us the warning. Uplink first keeps Garnir in the dark, but it is a long walk under their mortar. A quiet approach keeps the alarm waiting, and the warning with it.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief13": "The third is the dish field on the crater floor, beside the hab. That is what we are paid to break, and it will be the best defended. Their lander pad is beside it, and by Wayline's manifests that lander runs more than signal gear.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief14": "Two rim guns beside the mast cover the open ground; rockets or the Hound for those. Bunkers at the hab airlock and the foot of the uplink ramp, a rocket truck on the knoll. The boulder field to the north reaches the rim in cover. The rille to the south runs under the dishes.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief15": "One more thing. The riggers who built the post for Sable were never let go. They are kept in a module in the hab to hold the dishes in alignment. Pia Lindqvist runs the crew. Walk them back to our boats before the dishes blow, and their outfit will pay for it.",
	"corvusBlindWatchBrief16": "Charges on all three sites. Cover the planters, mind the order, and watch your air, all of you.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldAlarmShot": "Shots fired. The Sounding is awake, and the uplink will start talking to Garnir.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldAlarmSighted": "A sentry has us. The post is standing to. Expect the uplink to start sending.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldAlarmMast": "Their ranging mast has us. That is the alarm, and their mortar has a picture of the flat.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldWarningStarted": "The uplink is transmitting. That is Brannick calling Garnir. Stop it before it finishes, Captain, or Garnir knows we are coming.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldWarningHalf": "Half their warning is out. If the uplink matters, it matters now.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldWarningSent": "It went through. Garnir has their warning, and whoever waits there knows Wayline came to Warion. Finish the job. We pay for that one on Garnir.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldWarningStopped": "The warning is cut off. Garnir heard the start of it and nothing it can use.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldMastDown": "Mast is down. Their mortar fires on what its own crews can see now, which isn't much. Cross the flat.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldUplinkDown": "That is the uplink. Nothing more leaves Warion for Garnir.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldDishesDown": "The dish field is down. Their ears are gone, Captain. That is the contract.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldMortarDestroyed": "Mortar carrier is burning. No more shells on the flat.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldRiggersFound": "Found the riggers. Six of them in a module, door bolted from the outside. Lindqvist says they will walk if we lead, and she wants to know which way. Not past the pad, she says.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldRiggersMoving": "Riggers are out and moving. Their suits are work suits, no plate on them. Keep the way clear.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldRiggersOut": "Lindqvist's crew is at the boats. They have given us the post as they built it: the bunkers and the rover track are on your map now.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldRiggersLost": "The riggers aren't coming out. They built this place, and they stay in it. Keep going.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldScheduleFound": "Captain, the console in that control hut is still logged onto the uplink. Hold it and I can give Garnir a Wayline sailing schedule. Not a true one. It only works while the uplink stands and before their warning gets through.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldScheduleWorking": "The console is ours. Keep the leader on it, and keep the uplink standing until it is sent.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldScheduleSent": "Sent. Garnir is reading our sailings now, and every one of them is wrong. Let them wait for boats that never leave.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldScheduleLapsed": "The console is no use to us now. Garnir won't take a schedule from Warion.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldColdStoreFound": "Cryo pods, racked out on the surface past the lander pad, a medical tag on every one. That is Sable's other trade. Put a squad on the racks and log the manifest, Captain. A navy reads that kind of paper.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldColdStoreWorking": "We're on the racks, reading the tags into the log. Dates, weights, a buyer on Garnir for each. Nobody look any closer than that.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldColdStoreLogged": "The manifest is logged. Every pod, its tag, and who on Garnir was waiting for it. It earns us nothing. Keep it anyway; someone with a navy behind them will want it.",
	"corvusBlindWatchFieldStoodTo": "They are expecting us. Teague got off Asharu and told them. The watch is stood to, Captain. Assume they are awake from the first step.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefOpenQuiet": "The Sounding is silent, Zoey. Mast, uplink and dishes, all three. The uplink went down before Garnir heard anything it could use.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefOpenWarned": "The Sounding is silent, Zoey. Mast, uplink and dishes. But the uplink finished its warning first. Garnir knows we were on Warion.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefRoutingQuiet": "Fenner's racks kept their routing tables. Everything the post heard went one way: to Sable's dispatch compound on Garnir. And Garnir does not know we have seen them.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefRoutingWarned": "Fenner's racks kept their routing tables, and every one of them points to the dispatch compound on Garnir. Garnir has been told. We will find them awake.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefRoutingSchedule": "The routing tables point to Sable's dispatch compound on Garnir. And the last thing Garnir heard from Warion is a Wayline schedule I wrote. They will be watching for sailings that never leave.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefRiggersFreed": "Coldframe Rigging paid for their people, and Pia Lindqvist asked me to thank you by name. The crew that built that post walked off Warion.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefRiggersLeft": "The riggers are still on Warion, waiting on whoever Sable sends to pick through the wreck. We knew where they were.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefRiggersLost": "The riggers died on Warion. We found them and could not bring them out. I will remember that about this job.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefColdStoreLogged": "The cold store's manifest is in our files. It pays nothing, and I would rather not have read it. It stays there until someone who can act on it asks.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefCostLosses": "We chose the ground and the order, and we still left people on that moon. Their names go down before the plan for Garnir does.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebriefCostClean": "Everyone came back off Warion. That was preparation, and some of it was luck. We don't plan Garnir on luck.",
	"corvusColdAccountTitle": "A Cold Account",
	"corvusColdAccountBriefing": "We found their buyers on Asharu and blinded their listening post on Warion. Sable's dispatch compound on Garnir is the last link. Secure the marked pirate dispatch records and transmit the proof. The Hegemony has an Onslaught in the area. Give its captain proof of pirate ownership, and we can get the Navy to finish this for us. Withdraw every surviving squad and your Hound to the marked extraction point. The Onslaught will take station beyond the eastern perimeter. Get clear of the marked bombardment area and reach your pickup. Your shuttles will return for the survivors while the batteries demolish the stronghold. Board as soon as they land. The operation ends when the last shuttle carrying your survivors leaves the area; Resolute will finish its work on its own orders. Expect fortified positions and better-equipped crews; you do not need to clear the entire garrison.",
	"corvusColdAccountRequirements": "{0} squads and {1} mechs or vehicles recommended. Sable''s compound is walled and gated, with heavy guns, autocannon and a rocket battery inside it, two gun nests on the approach road, and point-defence mounts that shoot down incoming rockets. Their machines wait in the mech bays and roll out once your company is inside the compound: land rockets and anti-armour weapons, not rifles alone. Minimum: two squads with four ready marines each. Up to four fitted company shuttles can ferry the selected force. Wayline provides heavy lift for your active mech lance; select Mech Support. No fighter cover or employer infantry.",
	"corvusColdAccountDebrief": "The records proved the compound belonged to Sable. Your surviving company is clear. Resolute has its proof and its orders; you are not required to wait on the Navy's timetable. You have broken Sable's operation against Wayline in Corvus. Your company found the records, disabled their listening post and brought back the proof that released Resolute's guns. Those achievements belong to you. I mistook the Navy's interest for a partnership; it offered no promise beyond this operation. Wayline knows what your work is worth. Other crews will still work these lanes, and larger powers set their own terms. We have something to build on, and more reason to choose our contracts carefully.",
	"corvusFlavor": "{0}: {1}",
	"corvusRequirements": "{0} squads recommended. Minimum: two squads with four ready marines each. Up to four fitted company shuttles can ferry the selected force. Wayline provides heavy lift for your active mech lance; select Mech Support. No fighter cover or employer infantry.",
	"waylineSentenceJoin": " ",
	"corvusWaylineTitle": "WAYLINE / THE CORVUS ACCOUNT",
	"corvusIntroNoRoute": "Our dispatch records point beyond {0}.",
	"corvusIntroDelivered": "Dispatch has receipts for delivered loads: {0}. That is work Wayline can build on.",
	"corvusIntroLostLoads": "The lost loads remain on the ledger too.",
	"corvusIntroNoFreight": "No freight made it through. The depot is still ours, but this route has not recovered.",
	"corvusIntroRelayClosed": "The relay contract is closed. Its payment and your work remain on our books.",
	"corvusIntroTail": "When we met, Wayline was coming apart. You gave us room to act. See to your company first. The work on Asharu can wait until you are ready.",
	"districtEscortCampaignName": "District Escort",
	"districtEscortCampaignTerms": "Terms: {0} credits once, on delivery of this consignment with its party and your company at the western apron. No equipment award, premium, house promotion, MRB standing, stationing contract or faction commission; the signed agreement and its ratification are unchanged. Four district constables hold the apron. Two squads recommended; your fitted shuttles carry your selected marines. If the consignment or both of its party are lost, or the company withdraws, the job is unpaid and the next posting is a new consignment with new people.",
	"districtEscortCampaignRuskSender": "OFFICE OF BARONET ELIAN DORMER / CONCESSION SECURITY",
	"districtEscortCampaignRuskParty": "Dormer custodial clerk",
	"districtEscortCampaignRuskBrief": "Dormer''s office: Under the custody agreement, the concession ships its own freight on its own schedule. Consignment {0} leaves the Low Quay loading lane for the western apron with two of my custodial clerks, who sign it over at the gate. Raiders still work the freight lane; two pickets have been seen on it and more will come onto the lane once your shuttles are down. Meet the carrier, then keep it covered. My managers expect it delivered, not defended in place.",
	"districtEscortCampaignLennaSender": "LATCHKEY YARD ASSOCIATION / COMMON SERVICE DESK",
	"districtEscortCampaignLennaParty": "Association service delegate",
	"districtEscortCampaignLennaBrief": "Lenna Saye: The compact lets the benches ship common-service work without asking Dormer''s office for a lease. Consignment {0} is pump parts and recovered stock for the weir and the yard; two of our delegates travel with it and sign it over at the western apron. Raiders still work the freight lane. Two pickets sit on it, and more will come onto the lane once your shuttles are down. Meet the carrier at the loading lane and get it, and our people, across.",
	"districtEscortCampaignHistory": "Escort record: {0}. This posting is a new consignment with new people.",
	"districtEscortCampaignRequirements": "Two squads recommended; two selected squads with at least four ready marines each required. Up to four fitted company shuttles. Four constables and a two-person handover party. No tender or mech required.",
	"districtEscortCampaignDebriefWon": "{0}: The consignment is signed over at the apron. {1} credits paid. The next load is new freight and new people; post again when the company is ready.",
	"districtEscortCampaignDebriefLost": "{0}: The consignment did not arrive. No fee. Confirmed losses stay on record; the next posting is a new consignment with new people, not this load retried.",
	"waylineArcTitle": "WAYLINE / AN OPEN ROAD",
	"waylineProgressRelief": "CHAPTER 1 / 2 — RELIEF",
	"waylineProgressDepot": "RELIEF COMPLETE / CHAPTER 2 — THE DEPOT",
	"waylineProgressComplete": "RELIEF COMPLETE / DEPOT COMPLETE",
	"waylineIntroRelief": "Castle sent your particulars, and I've read them twice. I broker for Wayline, and since the spring I run it, because our director took a post off-world and somebody had to. A year ago we ran freighters between worlds. We lost three cargoes in a season and sold the hulls to cover them, so now we're drivers on one planet's roads, pooling what's left so nobody has to sell their truck as well.",
	"waylineIntroDepot": "You have bought us breathing room holding that checkpoint. Now I need your team to clear one of my freight depots so we can get our drivers back to work.",
	"waylineIntroComplete": "There's some recurring security work if you need it.",
	"waylineBriefingOnPlanet": " on {0}",
	"waylineBriefingRelief": "(A) Reinforce the checkpoint gate. No need to sally out these raiders seem motivated to rush the checkpoint.",
	"waylineBriefingCounterattack": "(A) Take and hold the warehouse.\n(B) Optional: find and activate the Hound to support your company.",
	"waylineDebriefReliefWon": "Thanks Commander. Your first payment from Wayline is cleared. I've got more \"delivery\" work when you're ready.",
	"waylineDebriefDepotWon": "The depot is ours again. Dispatch can start moving freight. Your payment is cleared.",
	"waylineDebriefHoundAward": "Crew brought that Hound to the mech bay. Looks like it needs some work. We found a spare SRM launcher in the packaging that needs to be installed.",
	"supplyRouteLabelConvoy": "CONVOY / BREAKTHROUGH",
	"supplyRouteLabelCapture": "CAPTURE / HOLD",
	"supplyRouteLabelOperation": "OPERATION",
	"supplyRouteJunctionName": "Open the Junction",
	"supplyRouteThunderName": "Thunder Run",
	"supplyRouteSecurityName": "Route Security",
	"supplyRouteJunctionTerms": "An allied gunship works the trenches ahead while your company takes the road.\n\n(A) Weigh Station: take the toll post.\n\n(B) Freight Yard: take the yard and its bonded warehouse.\n\n(C) Junction Dispatch: take dispatch, then hold all three.",
	"supplyRouteThunderTerms": "(A) Dispatch Post: clear it, then hold for 90 seconds.\n\n(B) East Crossing: take it and hold for 2 minutes against raiders from the cross streets.\n\n(C) Outbound Gate: secure it to start the freight run.\n\n(D) Exit checkpoint: the tank and APCs break the gun line. Keep the road open for the three loads.",
	"supplyRouteThunderPay": "Terms: Cr. 6,000, plus 4,000 per carrier delivered, up to 18,000.",
	"supplyRouteSecurityTerms": "Zoey Venn: Capture Power Yard, Freight Gate and Relay Hall, retaining the landing apron. Eight militia hold secured ground while your company pushes forward. A limited raider reserve will try to retake your gains. Wayline pays for each security job held.",
	"supplyRouteFreightLedger": "Freight ledger: {0}.",
	"supplyRouteRequirements": "2 squads recommended.",
	"supplyRouteRecoveryFreight": "The delivered loads are real work on Wayline's books again. The next contract takes us off-world, to Asharu, when you are ready.",
	"supplyRouteRecoveryJunction": "Credits paid and our junction is open. Once your company is ready, we put our freight through the corridor. We'll work on organizing our freight in the meantime.",
